    "originalReason": "ACCEPT_COMPLETE_BOUNDED_DESIGN. Both complete bilingual cases supply actual condensed structures for primary dihaloalkanes and OH-minus. Lone-pair attack on electrophilic primary C and C-Br pair departure to Br conserve valence; the O-H bond is retained and no extra proton relay is needed in the supplied OH-minus model. 1,6-dibromohexane plus2OH-minus gives1,6-hexanediol plus2Br-minus; 1,3-dibromopropane likewise gives1,3-propanediol. Both overall charges are minus2 and all atoms are retained. Explicit concerted primary-C substitution is a stipulated simplified model, not a sole-pathway/yield claim. Bromoethane transfer changes functionality to a monofunctional alcohol. In the stopped-X case its exact identity is supplied, and one-equivalent mean dosage is correctly insufficient to infer every molecule is singly converted. These are genuine separately graded functionality/mechanism inferences; chain-length relabelling alone is not counted as transfer. Both12point rubrics demand all four expectations. A bare overall equation cannot substitute for both local electron-pair sequences. The tasks do not claim actual synthesis or compare SN1/SN2 kinetics. Actual independent original-design review only. No learner execution, Human approval, authoritative kind transport, native D/V, whole-course source or acquisition clearance.",
