    "originalReason": "The new DE/EN descriptions explicitly require performing and evaluating selected reducing-carbohydrate and glucose assays and explaining their differing analytical scope through molecular structure and enzyme action. The performance operator remains; no requirement to execute every example method is introduced.\n\nThe existing structure-and-evidence, fresh-transfer and execution expectations all remain necessary and supported at design level. New wording states their existing analytic distinction; it does not add a disconnected fourth skill or waive the practical evidence needed for an individual mastery decision.\n\nThe previously actually read manufacturer method and its limits remain relevant: a 1 percent mass/volume sugar loading is10000mg/L and can exceed the GOD strip range. The existing case explicitly calls for dilution when scale is exceeded. Separate suitable GOD aliquots and the manufacturer timing/pH conditions remain required; hot alkaline Benedict mixtures do not become valid GOD samples. No laboratory execution has been observed here.\n\nAll source routes, case texts and own prerequisites are unchanged. The literal contribution/source-track boundaries of the prior review remain; no entire jurisdiction or course is approved. Existing memory_required and original card duty remain without a new M vote.",
