    "originalReason": "Both complete DE/EN cases are soluble: alanine yields L with D mirror; glycine has two H and no D/L pair. The rotated cysteine input becomes L after the permitted180-degree paper turn; new serine is D. The90-degree renewed Fischer reading reverses configuration; physical rotation of a molecule does not interconvert enantiomers. D/L gives no rotation sign. Both12-point rubrics and fresh transfer match the goal. Current independently inspected native page, source/prerequisite context and materials support this unchanged complete profile. Frozen first judgment: curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-16/chemie-native9-current437-fresh-independent-a-20261016-v1/FIRST.independent-current-nine-science-and-separate699.frozen.json sha256:dbdbefe4b37fa1dc2d314b647d1a275d81715783a9c2b6c76ef17ce846d97d4a",
